    {
      "title": "Link Settings",
      "desc": "LCP agrees on size and login",
      "detail": "Now PPP runs inside the session, starting with LCP. Each side asks for its settings: packets of at most 1,492 bytes, since PPPoE’s 8 bytes have to fit in Ethernet’s 1,500, and a random magic number to spot loops. The server also asks for a CHAP login. Both agree.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Largest packet",
          "1,492 bytes (MRU)"
        ],
        [
          "Login",
          "CHAP with MD5"
        ],
        [
          "Ethernet type",
          "0x8864 (session)"
        ]
      ],
